<!--Render Target Documentation — SetRendering
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.SetRendering-->
<rdoc:SetRendering xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Set processor: STEPS, bounding box, and view submodules
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A block whose baseType chain includes com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set is
    rendered by ScadSetProcessor as a SCAD file with a STEPS array and four
    view submodules.

    A MachineBlocks set uses three aggregations. _presets and _parts are
    inherited. _steps is declared on Set.

    - _presets — palette; configurations referenced by appliedPresets on _parts
    - _parts — placed instances (direction, offset, appliedPresets; id becomes
      the SCAD instance id)
    - _steps — assembly order; optional; default is _parts document order

    STEPS is generated from the placement list. Each entry:

        [instanceId, boundingBox, direction, offset]

    - [0] instanceId — string from the placed instance id
    - [1] boundingBox — [x, y, z] from the instance size literal, otherwise
      the placed type's size property default. Preset merge is not applied.
    - [2] direction — "west" | "north" | "east" | "south"
    - [3] offset — [x, y, z]

    Example:

        STEPS = [
            ["00001", [16, 16, 1], "west", [0, 0, 0]],
            ["00002", [4, 4, 9], "west", [0, 0, 1]]
        ];

    The set bounding box is computed at SCAD render time by the Core function
    mb_parts_total_size, which reads size, direction, and offset from each
    STEPS row:

        ["size", mb_parts_total_size(STEPS)]

    Four submodules, PascalCase suffixes of the set module:

        ...DefaultEnclosure__Total
        ...DefaultEnclosure__Print
        ...DefaultEnclosure__Step
        ...DefaultEnclosure__Instance

    The Instance submodule dispatches with if / else if on instanceId to
    per-instance modules named with the id appended by underscore
    (...__Instance_00001). Each of those modules calls the manifestation
    module of the placed part's type FQN with config and settings for size,
    offset, and direction. mb_block applies that offset and direction. The
    set does not add a translate around the call. STEPS feeds only
    mb_parts_total_size.

    Total and Print call every instance module in STEPS order. Step calls the
    prefix of that list whose index is less than or equal to the customizer
    variable step. When _steps is absent, STEPS follows _parts document order.
    A missing direction defaults to "west". A missing offset defaults to
    [0, 0, 0]. A missing id or size returns files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_SET_PART_INCOMPLETE.

    Set customizer variables:

        mode       = "total"; // [total:Total, print:3D Print, step:Step, instance:Instance]
        step       = 0;       // [0:9]
        instanceId = "00001";
        assembly   = "merged"; // [unassembled:Unassembled, assembled:Assembled, merged:Merged]
        baseColor  = "#EAC645";

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Customizer" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:SetRendering>
